                          "fill": "#C3B5AE",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": 820,
                          "content": "Issue 1 inverted to a cool carbon grey with a light blue accent. Issue 2 inverts to a warm brown-black with the oxblood reading as a light terracotta — the same hue rotated for a dark ground, because a deep oxblood on near-black is unreadable. On paper the accent carries cream text; on the dark ground it carries dark text. That inversion is the only structural difference between the two themes.",
